            <ArticleTitle>Suprasellar tension pneumocyst after transsphenoidal surgery. Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>146-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tension pneumocephalus is an uncommon occurrence after transsphenoidal surgery. The author presents an unusual case of postoperative visual deterioration related to expanding air within a suprasellar tumor cavity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
